# FRIDAY

## Function Manual

Friday is an AI desktop assistant that accepts voice and text input and provides text and voice responses. Use the following prompts to access its features.

## 1. Voice and Conversation

### Voice Input

Press F2 to toggle the microphone. This shortcut works while Friday is minimized, provided the application is still running.

Examples:

- "Set my volume to 40 percent."
- "Open YouTube."
- "Explain what machine learning is."

### General Conversation

Ask questions or request explanations, advice, and general assistance.

Examples:

- "What is the difference between AI and machine learning?"
- "Explain how an API works."
- "Give me tips to improve my productivity."

## 2. Browser Module

### Open a Website

Opens a website in your browser.

Examples:

- "Open YouTube."
- "Open GitHub."
- "Open [https://www.wikipedia.org](https://www.wikipedia.org)."

### Search a Specific Website

Searches a supported website and opens its search results.

Supported websites: YouTube, Google, GitHub, Wikipedia, Reddit, Amazon, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter/X, and Spotify.

Examples:

- "Search YouTube for Python tutorials."
- "Search GitHub for React projects."
- "Search Wikipedia for artificial intelligence."

### Summarize a Webpage

Extracts webpage text, summarizes its content, and saves the summary as a text file in your Downloads folder.

Examples:

- "Summarize this webpage: [https://example.com/article](https://example.com/article)."
- "Summarize this article: [https://example.com/news](https://example.com/news)."
- "Give me a summary of [https://example.com/research](https://example.com/research)."

### Compose an Email

Generates an email subject and body, then opens Gmail and enters the draft.

Examples:

- "Compose an email requesting leave for tomorrow."
- "Draft an email to my professor asking for an assignment extension."
- "Write a professional email thanking the interviewer."

Note: Friday prepares the draft; review it and send it yourself.

## 3. Desktop Module

### Volume Control

Sets the system volume to the requested level.

Examples:

- "Set the volume to 30 percent."
- "Increase the volume to 70 percent."
- "Set the volume to 0 percent."

### Brightness Control

Sets the screen brightness to the requested level.

Examples:

- "Set brightness to 50 percent."
- "Reduce brightness to 25 percent."
- "Set brightness to 80 percent."

### Take a Screenshot

Captures a screenshot of the screen.

Examples:

- "Take a screenshot."
- "Capture my screen."
- "Take a screenshot of what is currently displayed."

### Create a Folder

Creates a folder using a saved or specified parent folder.

Examples:

- "Create a folder named Projects inside Documents."
- "Create a folder named DSA inside Desktop."
- "Create a folder named Notes inside folder D."

### Create a File

Creates a file in the specified or saved folder. Content can be included in the request.

Examples:

- "Create a file named notes.txt in Documents."
- "Create a file named ideas.txt in Desktop with the content: Friday project ideas."
- "Create a file named empty.txt in Downloads."

### Open a File

Opens a file from the specified or saved folder.

Examples:

- "Open notes.txt in folder Documents."
- "Open report.pdf in folder Downloads."
- "Open resume.docx in folder Desktop."

### Open a Folder

Opens a folder, optionally specifying its parent folder.

Examples:

- "Open Projects inside Documents."
- "Open Downloads."
- "Open the folder named DSA."

### Search for a File

Searches for a file inside the specified parent folder.

Examples:

- "Search for notes.txt inside folder Documents."
- "Find report.pdf inside folder Downloads."
- "Search for resume.docx inside folder Desktop."

### Search for a Folder

Searches for a folder inside the specified parent folder.

Examples:

- "Search for folder Projects inside Documents."
- "Find folder DSA inside folder Desktop."
- "Search for folder Reports inside folder Downloads."

### Rename a File

Renames a file in the specified folder.

Examples:

- "Rename notes.txt in Documents to study_notes.txt."
- "Rename report.pdf in Downloads to final_report.pdf."
- "Rename draft.docx in Desktop to final.docx."

### Rename a Folder

Renames a folder, with or without specifying its parent folder.

Examples:

- "Rename folder Projects inside folder Documents to Work."
- "Rename folder DSA to DataStructures."
- "Rename folder Reports inside folder Desktop to OldReports."

### Move a File

Moves a file from its source folder to a destination folder.

Examples:

- "Move notes.txt from folder Desktop to folder Documents."
- "Move report.pdf from folder Downloads to folder Desktop."
- "Move resume.docx from folder Documents to folder Downloads."

### Move a Folder

Moves a folder to another destination.

Examples:

- "Move Projects from folder Desktop to folder Documents."
- "Move folder DSA to folder Documents."
- "Move Reports from folder Downloads to folder Desktop."

### Delete a File

Deletes the specified file.

Examples:

- "Delete notes.txt in folder Documents."
- "Delete report.pdf in folder Downloads."
- "Delete draft.docx in folder Desktop."

### Delete a Folder

Deletes a folder, optionally specifying its parent folder.

Examples:

- "Delete folder Projects inside folder Documents."
- "Delete folder DSA."
- "Delete folder OldReports inside folder Desktop."

Important: Verify the target carefully before requesting deletion.

### Close a File

Closes a file by its filename.

Examples:

- "Close notes.txt."
- "Close report.pdf."
- "Close resume.docx."

### Open a Local Application

Opens an installed application by its display name.

Examples:

- "Open Notepad."
- "Open Calculator."
- "Open Visual Studio Code."

Availability depends on the application's name and how it is registered or recognized on your system.

### Paste Content

Pastes generated or requested text into the currently focused application.

Examples:

- "Paste a short paragraph about artificial intelligence."
- "Write a Python hello-world program and paste it."
- "Paste a professional introduction for my presentation."

Make sure the intended application and input field are focused before using this function.

### Open Selected URL

Opens the URL currently selected on the screen.

Examples:

- "Open the selected URL."
- "Open this selected link."
- "Launch the URL I selected."

### Open Selected Path

Opens the file or folder path currently selected on the screen.

Examples:

- "Open the selected path."
- "Open the file path I selected."
- "Open the selected folder location."

### Analyze Selected Content

Explains, rewrites, or verifies the text selected by the user. Friday uses the selected content automatically.

Examples:

- "Explain the selected text."
- "Rewrite the selected paragraph professionally."
- "Verify the selected content for accuracy."

### Analyze the Screen

Analyzes the current screen using a screenshot and answers a question about its contents.

Examples:

- "Analyze my screen and explain what is displayed."
- "Look at the current screen and explain this error."
- "Describe the information visible on my screen."

## 4. System Power Controls

### Shutdown

Shuts down the computer when explicitly requested.

Examples:

- "Shut down my computer."
- "Turn off my PC."
- "Perform a system shutdown."

### Restart

Restarts the computer when explicitly requested.

Examples:

- "Restart my computer."
- "Restart my PC."
- "Perform a system restart."

### Lock the Computer

Locks the current session.

Examples:

- "Lock my computer."
- "Lock the screen."
- "Lock my PC now."

### Sleep

Puts the computer into sleep mode.

Examples:

- "Put my computer to sleep."
- "Make my PC sleep."
- "Perform a sleep operation."

### Hibernate

Puts the computer into hibernation.

Examples:

- "Hibernate my computer."
- "Put my PC into hibernation."
- "Perform system hibernation."

## 5. Persistent Memory and Folder Management

Friday stores user preferences and saved folder locations locally, allowing you to refer to saved folders by name rather than repeatedly providing full paths.

### Save a Folder Location

1. Open the folder management interface.
2. Use the folder picker to select a folder.
3. Press Insert Path to save its name and location.

### View Saved Folders

View saved folder names and locations in the table.

### Search Saved Folders

Find a saved folder entry using the available search interface.

### Delete a Saved Folder Entry

Remove a saved folder location from Friday's memory using the interface. This is separate from deleting the actual folder from your computer.

### Automatic Path Maintenance

When a saved folder is renamed, moved, or deleted through supported operations, Friday updates or removes affected saved paths as appropriate.

### Case-Insensitive Folder Names

Friday treats folder names such as DSA, dsa, and Dsa as the same name.

## 6. PDF Assistant

Switch to PDF Retrieval Mode to ask questions about uploaded PDF documents.

### Upload PDFs

Upload the documents you want Friday to use.

### Ask Questions About PDFs

Ask questions about the content of the available documents.

Examples:

- "Summarize the main points of this PDF."
- "Explain the methodology described in the document."
- "What conclusions does this research paper present?"

### Find Specific Information

Ask Friday to retrieve relevant details from your uploaded documents.

Examples:

- "What problem does this paper attempt to solve?"
- "Explain the proposed architecture in the document."
- "Compare the methods discussed in these documents."

Friday uses locally generated embeddings and retrieval to find relevant document content before generating an answer. Processing capacity depends on your computer's resources and the application's configured limits.

## 7. Important Notes

- Use General Mode for conversation, desktop operations, and browser operations.
- Use PDF Retrieval Mode for questions about uploaded PDFs.
- Use saved folder locations to simplify file and folder commands.
- Press F2 to toggle the microphone while Friday is running.
- Review email drafts before sending them.
- Check filenames and folder names before moving, renaming, or deleting items.
- Friday stores uploaded PDFs, saved folder locations, and preferences locally. However, AI features that use Groq may send relevant input to the cloud service for processing.
